IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `era-types`
IMPORT `era-access`
IMPORT `era-dates`

-- Employment Relations Act 2000 — GOALS 2 AND 3: TIME LIMITS AND REMEDIES.
--
--   "Was the grievance raised in time; by when must proceedings begin; and
--    what remedies are available?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2000_24.txt — ss 114, 120,
-- 123B-124, 128, 142.

§ `Goal 2 — raising a grievance and time limits`

-- s 114 "(7) ... employee notification period means,— (a) in respect of a
-- personal grievance under section 103(1)(d), the period of 12 months
-- beginning with the date on which the action alleged to amount to the
-- personal grievance occurred or came to the notice of the employee,
-- whichever is later: (b) in respect of any other personal grievance, the
-- period of 90 days beginning with the date [likewise]". A period beginning
-- with day S includes S: 90 days end on S + 89; 12 months end under the
-- Legislation Act 2019 s 56 (the day before the corresponding day, or the end
-- of the month if there is none: changed after the independent pass). Legislation Act 2019 s 55: a last day that is not a working
-- day moves to the next working day (fork F3).
@ref s 114(7)
@export The last day to raise a personal grievance with the employer under s 114 of the Employment Relations Act 2000 (NZ): 90 days beginning with the later of the action and the employee learning of it (12 months for sexual harassment). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN g IS A Grievance  @desc The ground, and when the action occurred and came to the employee's notice
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to raise the grievance` g MEANS
    `the last day under s 55 for a period ending on` plain `, Matariki days` (g's `Matariki Observance Days`)
    WHERE
        plain MEANS
            IF   g's `ground` EQUALS `(d) sexual harassment`
            THEN `the last day of a period of` 12 `months beginning with` start
            ELSE `the day` 89 `days after` start
        start MEANS
            IF   g's `action came to the employee's notice on` GREATER THAN g's `action occurred on`
            THEN g's `action came to the employee's notice on`
            ELSE g's `action occurred on`

-- s 114 "(1) An employee who wishes to raise a personal grievance must ...
-- raise the grievance with their employer within the applicable employee
-- notification period unless the employer consents to the personal grievance
-- being raised after the expiration of that period. ... (4) ... the Authority
-- ... may grant leave".
@ref s 114(1), (3)-(4)
GIVEN g IS A Grievance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grievance was raised in time` g IF
        g's `grievance raised on` AT MOST `the last day to raise the grievance` g
    OR  g's `employer consented to late raising`
    OR  g's `Authority granted leave under s 114(4)`

-- s 114 "(6) No action may be commenced in the Authority or the court in
-- relation to a personal grievance more than 3 years after the date on which
-- the personal grievance was raised". s 142 "No action may be commenced ...
-- in relation to an employment relationship problem that is not a personal
-- grievance more than 6 years after the date on which the cause of action
-- arose." Each extended under Legislation Act 2019 s 55.
@ref ss 114(6), 142
GIVEN raised IS A DATE
      matariki IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to commence an action on a grievance raised on` raised `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    `the last day under s 55 for a period ending on` (`add years` raised 3) `, Matariki days` matariki

@ref s 142
GIVEN arose IS A DATE
      matariki IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to commence another action, cause arising on` arose `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    `the last day under s 55 for a period ending on` (`add years` arose 6) `, Matariki days` matariki

-- s 120 "(1) Where an employee is dismissed, that employee may, within 60
-- days after the dismissal or within 60 days after the employee has become
-- aware of the dismissal, whichever is the later, request the employer to
-- provide a statement in writing of the reasons for the dismissal. (2) Every
-- employer ... must, within 14 days after the day on which the request is
-- received, provide the statement".
@ref s 120
GIVEN dismissed IS A DATE, aware IS A DATE
      matariki IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to request reasons for a dismissal on` dismissed `, learned of on` aware `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    `the last day under s 55 for a period ending on` (`the day` 60 `days after` (IF aware GREATER THAN dismissed THEN aware ELSE dismissed)) `, Matariki days` matariki

@ref s 120(2)
GIVEN received IS A DATE
      matariki IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to give the statement of reasons, request received` received `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    `the last day under s 55 for a period ending on` (`the day` 14 `days after` received) `, Matariki days` matariki

§ `Goal 3 — remedies`

-- s 123B "the Authority or the court must not provide for any remedy if ...
-- (a) an action of the employee contributed to the situation ...; and (b)
-- that action amounts to serious misconduct." s 123C: "must not provide for
-- ... (a) the remedy in section 123(1)(a) [reinstatement]: (b) the remedy in
-- section 123(1)(c) [compensation]" if the employee contributed.
@ref ss 123B, 123C
GIVEN r IS A `Remedy facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reinstatement and compensation are available` r IF
    NOT r's `the employee contributed to the situation`

-- s 128 "(2) ... the Authority must ... order the employer to pay to the
-- employee the lesser of a sum equal to that lost remuneration or to 3
-- months' ordinary time remuneration." "subject to ... section 124": "(1) ...
-- reduce the remedies ... accordingly. (2) Remedies may be reduced ... by up
-- to 100%." s 123B: nothing if the contribution was serious misconduct.
@ref ss 123B, 124, 128(2)
@export The reimbursement of lost remuneration the Authority must order on a successful personal grievance under s 128 of the Employment Relations Act 2000 (NZ): the lesser of the remuneration lost and 3 months' ordinary time remuneration, reduced by the percentage for the employee's contribution (s 124), and nothing if the contribution amounted to serious misconduct (s 123B). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Remedy facts`  @desc Contribution, serious misconduct, the percentage reduction, lost remuneration, and 3 months' ordinary time remuneration
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reimbursement the Authority must order` r MEANS
    IF   r's `the employee contributed to the situation` AND r's `the contribution amounts to serious misconduct`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF   reduction GREATER THAN 100 OR reduction LESS THAN 0
         THEN `s 124(2) allows a reduction of 0% to 100% only`
         ELSE min (r's `remuneration lost`) (r's `3 months' ordinary time remuneration`) TIMES (1 MINUS reduction DIVIDED BY 100)
    WHERE
        reduction MEANS r's `reduction for contribution, in percent`

`s 124(2) allows a reduction of 0% to 100% only` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 124(2): remedies may be reduced by up to 100%"

